From 00ceb90ad0d0b1f0c15ef2f832d113a8dd891b75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: csolomon <charliesolomon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:47:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] deps: vitest 4.1.9 -> 4.1.11 (GHSA-82fw-gwwq-j7x9, #93)

Why a patch: this is a change to upstream's dependency manifests and
lockfile, which no policy-pack extension can express. Upstream still pins
vitest 4.1.9 on main at the time of writing; retire this patch at the
first sync whose upstream pin is >= 4.1.11.

What: `npm audit` in vendor/pi reports @vitest/mocker < 4.1.11 (path
traversal via redirect mock, moderate) through vitest and
@vitest/coverage-v8. vitest is a dev dependency in ten workspace
manifests; it never reaches the runtime bundle or a deployment package,
and GAH's CI audits runtime deps only (`--omit=dev`), so this closes the
finding for anyone running the full audit rather than a production
exposure.

How: the ten manifests pin 4.1.11; package-lock.json is updated in place
for the nine @vitest family entries (version/resolved/integrity from the
registry, plus their internal version ranges and the workspace
devDependencies), because npm 10.9 crashes on this tree
(#loadPeerSet: edgesOut of null) and npm 12 rewrites the whole file.
The 4.1.9 -> 4.1.11 graph differs only in those internal ranges, so the
edit is complete. Verified: `npm ci --ignore-scripts` accepts the
lockfile, `npm audit` is clean, vitest 4.1.11 runs the telemetry and
coding-agent suites, `make smoke` passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BGfxFj8Q1RT85fHaUGpoet

Re-authored 2026-09-22 (sync to v0.87.1): upstream still pins 4.1.9; the
lockfile context moved. Same nine registry entries, now eleven manifests.
